1. वप् cl. 1. P. Ā. व॑पति, ˚ते (only pres. stem and ind.p. उप्त्वा, -उप्य), to shear, shave (Ā. ‘one's self’), cut off, AV.; TS.; Br.; GṛŚrS.;
to crop (herbage), mow, cut (grass), graze, RV. vi, 6, 4 :
Caus. वापयति, ˚ते (Pot. वापयीत, ĀśvŚr.), to cause (Ā. ‘one's self’) to be shorn, GṛŚrS.

2. वप् cl. 1. P. Ā. (Dhātup. xxiii, 34) व॑पति, ˚ते (Pot. उपेत्, GṛS.; pf. उवाप, ऊपुः॑; ऊपे, RV. &c.; ववाप, MBh.; -वेपे, Kāś. on Pāṇ. vi, 4, 120; aor. अवाप्सीत्, Br. &c.;अवप्त Gr.; Pot. उप्यात्, ib.; fut. वप्ता, ib.; वप्स्य॑ति, Br.; वपिष्यति, MBh. &c.; inf. वप्तुम् Gr.; ind.p. उप्त्वा, MBh.; -उ॑प्य, RV. &c.),
to strew, scatter (esp. seed), sow, bestrew, RV. &c. &c.;
to throw, cast (dice), ib.;
to procreate, beget (see वपुस् and 2. वप्तृ);
to throw or heap up, dam up, AV. :
Pass. उप्य॑ते (aor. वापि, Br.), to be strewn or sown, RV. &c. &c.:
Caus. वापयति (aor. अवीवपत् Gr.) to sow, plant, put in the ground, MBh. :
Desid. विवप्सति, ˚ते Gr.:
Intens. वावप्यते, वावप्ति, ib.
